course: dictionary
lesson: 5734
title: Loss: losing, losing a game, and grief
level: primary-5
stars: 0
explain: Loss is a noun, and it comes from the word lose. It can mean losing something, having less of something, losing a game, losing money, or the sadness after someone dies. The sentence around it shows which meaning is right.
explain: «Noah quit matches just before he lost so they would not count, until the group made a rule: quitting counts as a loss.» Here a loss is a defeat in a game. Ask: what would fit here? A defeat fits, and a present does not.
explain: «At a self-checkout you scan your own shopping, and it is easy to miss something by accident; if you spot it, scan it, because an unpaid loaf of bread is a loss to the shop.» Here loss is about money. The shop gets less money back than it should. Check by swapping in "less money": it still makes sense.
explain: «Places such as a grandparent's house hold memories, so losing them can feel like another loss.» Here loss means a sad feeling, the grief that comes when something precious is gone. Bricks and mortar just means a building, but the memories are what hurts to lose.
fact: Loss means losing something, or having less of something.
fact: A loss is also when a team does not win a game.
fact: In money, a loss means you get back less than you paid.
fact: A loss can mean the death of someone, and the sadness that comes with it.
fact: "At a loss" means not knowing what to do.
exercise: «An unpaid loaf of bread is a loss to the shop.» What kind of loss is this? | Losing a friend | A team losing a match | *Less money than the shop should get | Losing an argument
exercise: Which phrase means "not knowing what to do"? | Hearing loss | *At a loss | Make a loss | Weight loss
exercise: «Losing the memories of her grandma's house can feel like another loss.» What feeling does loss show here? | Money | *Sadness | Hunger | Excitement
test: What does "make a loss" mean in money? | You get back more than you paid | You give your money away as a gift | You win a prize | *You get back less than you paid
test: Which word is the opposite of loss in money lessons? | Weight | Defeat | *Profit | Grief
exam: Which sentence uses loss to mean sadness? | The team had a loss in the final. | *After her grandad died, the loss made her quiet. | The shop had a loss on bread.
